<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sparrenburg</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sparrenburg Castle</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sparrenburg is a castle on a ridge of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutoburg-forest">Teutoburg Forest</a> above <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bielefeld">Bielefeld</a>, built by the counts of Ravensberg in the first half of the 13th century. It was the administrative seat of the county and was rebuilt as a fortress with bastions in the 16th century. Its tower and walls, restored in modern times, are a landmark of the city.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sparrenburg.jpg" alt="Sparrenburg" width="320" height="251" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Daniel Schwen · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bi_Sparrenburg_pano.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
